\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Polish reserves flat in Sept despite  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2011\par 14:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Reserves suggest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were small\par \par \uc2 * Belka says \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  unable to stop a prevailing trend\par \par \uc2 * Cbank may limit speedy depreciation, curb speculation - Belka\par \par \uc2 (Updates with cbank governor, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Oct 7 (Reuters) - Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves\par \par \uc2 were unchanged in September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday, suggesting its two \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the month were relatively small in size.\par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at 74.1 billion euros at the end of September, roughly the same as at the end of August.\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the market to defend the zloty in September for the first time in more than a decade, twice selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and buying zlotys, boosting the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than 2 percent to the euro.\par \par \uc2 The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in October, but it has not disclosed the amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  it sold on the market.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Marek Belka reiterated in an article published after the data that the bank would not defend any given level of the zloty and would not be able to reverse its falling trend if capital exits emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 "If the trend is such that some categories of capital exit emerging markets, including Poland, we will not be able to do much anyway," Belka was quoted as saying by obserwatorfinasowy.pl, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's news website.\par \par \uc2 "We can only ensure that the process is not rapid, that the temperature of this phenomenon is not increased by speculative actions," he said.\par \par \uc2 Poland's economy will not avoid a slowdown, but it does not have to be as deep as elsewhere in Europe, Belka added.\par \par \uc2 Poland was the only country to avoid a slowdown in the European Union in 2009. Analysts polled by Reuters forecast the economy to expand at 3.1 percent in 2012, down from 4.0 percent seen for 2011.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  SMALL?\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reports the value of its reserves at the end of each month in zlotys, euros and dollars, but it does not publish the allocation in particular \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This, economists say, makes it difficult to calculate the exact value of the September \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which they estimate at anywhere from 350 million to 1.5 billion euros.\par \par \uc2 "The very fact they are in the market at all is highly significant but versus average daily turnover (about 5 billion euros), that much for two days of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a small fraction," said Peter Attard Montalto, an emerging markets analyst at Nomura.\par \par \uc2 The zloty traded up 0.3 percent to the euro on Friday as better-than-expected jobs data in the U.S. boosted investors' risk appetite. The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is presently over 2 percent stronger than at the time of the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  two weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 Montalto added that larger \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  often account for 20-25 percent of daily turnover. At the lower end of estimates, \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounted to about 3.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 The bank had around 64 billion euros in securities denominated in convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August and gold worth around 4 billion euros at the end of September, the bank's data showed. During September U.S. and German treasury bonds gained in price, but gold fell.\par \par \uc2 More details regarding reserve assets of the National Bank of Poland are available on its website at:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.nbp.pl/homen.aspx?f=/en/statystyka/rez_of.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.nbp.pl/homen.aspx?f=/en/statystyka/rez_of.html}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.nbp.pl/homen.aspx?f=/en/statystyka/template.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.nbp.pl/homen.aspx?f=/en/statystyka/template.html}}}\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Marcin Goettig, Additional reporting by Dagmara Leszkowicz; Editing by Hugh Lawson)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-RESERVES/  (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111010e7a7000s0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
