\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Euro-Zone Issues Still In Focus\b0\par\par\uc2 By Leos Rousek   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2011\par 05:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par    Local/GMT \par  \par    0900/0700 Czech August retail sales \par    0900/0700 Hungary September industrial output data \par    1130/0930 Hungary three-year, five-year, 10-year government bond auction \par       N/A    Slovak coalition government leaders in talks over EFSF \par       N/A    Hungarian development minister in talks with Russia's first deputy prime minister \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro-zone issues and market moves in western Europe will overshadow run-of-the-mill economic indicators due out Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 In Slovakia, talks among leaders in the four party coalition government over their divisions about the approval for boosting the European Financial Stability Facility, the euro zone's rescue fund, will continue later Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The focus of the talks will likely be on whether the government can carry out the EFSF parliamentary vote as planned for next Tuesday even if the pro-bailout coalition parties have to rely on support from the country's opposition. The left-of-center Smer-Social Democrats, the largest opposition party, demands cabinet reshuffles in exchange for their support.\par \par \uc2 All 17 euro-zone members have to endorse changes to the EUR400 billion EFSF, designed to stem the euro debt crisis, for it to take effect.\par \par \uc2 In Hungary, the August industrial output reading is seen showing a mere 2% annual growth.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         Latest     Previous   %Chg    Daily   Daily    %Chg \par         0250 GMT   2150 GMT           High    Low     12/31 \par EUR/CZK 24.703-49 24.708-81  -0.08   24.766   24.734  -1.30 \par EUR/HUF 296.70-7.40 296.40-7.08 +0.10 297.08  296.92  +6.75 \par EUR/PLN 4.3773-854 4.3773-859 -0.01 4.3861   4.3824 +10.73 \par  \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par          Hungary        Poland          Czech Republic \par        Wed    Tue     Wed     Tue       Wed     Tue \par 3 yrs 7.23%  7.47%   4.43%   4.46%(1)  1.79%   1.80%(2) \par 5 yrs 7.70%  7.97%   5.22%   5.30%     2.00%   2.00% \par 10yrs 8.10%  8.46%   5.87%   5.94%     3.19%   3.19% \par (1) 2Yrs (2) 4Yrs \par  \par  \par  \par STOCKS \par EU Enlarged 15           1,712.59 gain  50.20 up 3.02% \par WIG 20                   2,144.87 gain  55.03 up 2.63% \par BUX                      16,457.60 gain 883.05 up 5.67% \par PX                       899.40   gain  8.20 up 0.92% \par  \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Poland's conservative opposition leader Jaroslaw Kaczynski said Wednesday he would sue German media for misrepresenting stinging criticism of Berlin he made in a new book.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 POLAND\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : The National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the zloty to prevent the market from destabilizing, but it has no particular exchange rate target, Governor Marek Belka told a press conference Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Rate increases the National Bank of Poland has implemented so far this year should be enough to bring consumer price inflation back to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's 2.5% target, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said after its monetary panel left interest rates unchanged Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SLOVAKIA: Slovakia's opposition Smer-Social Democracy party said Wednesday it won't vote in favor of expanding the powers of the euro zone's rescue fund next Tuesday, but instead will seek a government reshuffle in exchange for the party's support for changes to the fund in a possible repeat vote.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Magyar RTL Televizio Zrt., the Hungarian arm of \f28 \uc2 \f2 RTL Group SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (RTL.BT), received regulatory clearance Wednesday for two acquisitions which will expand its television channel portfolio. \f28 \uc2 \f2 RTL Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is owned by German broadcaster \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bertelsmann AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Leos Rousek, Dow Jones Newswires; +420 222 315 290; leos.rousek@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Marcin Sobczyk in Warsaw and Veronika Gulyas in Budapest also contributed to this briefing.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe}}}\uc2 \f2  for the new Dow Jones blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 10-05-11 2311ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020111006e7a60000m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
