rogram Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exists\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 10:26 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  So Far Were To Calm Market Down\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 10:27 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Work Agaist Inflationary Pressure\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 10:28 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Won't Allow \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  To Work Against General Policy\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 10:30 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Market Should Follow MPC, Not Other Way Round\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 10:30 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Stability Of Interest Rates Is Value In Itself\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 10:31 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: We'll Change Rates When Needed\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 10:31 EDT *DJ  NBP Belka: Conservative Stance On Rates Good Amid Instability\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 10:33 EDT *DJ  National Bank Of Poland Ends Conference On Rates\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 10:45 EDT DJ  National Bank Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  May Continue Zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  may continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the zloty to prevent the market from destabilizing, but it has no particular exchange rate target, Governor Marek Belka told a press conference Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "Such actions are possible still," he said when asked if the bank would again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has been weakened by the euro-zone sovereign debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 The zloty is detached from fundamentals, he also said, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains a tightening bias in monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely keep a conservative stance on rates, whose stability is a "value in itself," although the rates panel will change rates when needed, Belka said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday kept interest rates unchanged, saying tightening so far this year should be enough to bring elevated consumer price inflation, at 4.3% on year in August, to the 2.5% target.\par \par \uc2 -By Marcin Sobczyk, Dow Jones Newswires; +48 22 447 2432; marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 05, 2011 10:45 ET (14:45 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111005e7a5004dd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
