\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2  keeps rates steady,  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  in focus\b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2011\par 13:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rates last raised in June\par \par \uc2 * Analysts expect rate cuts next year\par \par \uc2 * Market awaiting comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds economist quote, details)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Oct 5 - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its key interest rate unchanged at 4.50 percent on Wednesday as widely expected, as it seeks to balance the impact of a weakening zloty on inflation against a looming economic slowdown.\par \par \uc2 All 23 analysts polled by Reuters had predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would leave borrowing costs unchanged after raising rates by a total 100 basis points this year, most recently in June.\par \par \uc2 The zloty and bonds did not show any reaction.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release its post-decision statement at 1400 GMT, when it also holds a monthly news conference.\par \par \uc2 Investors are hoping the bank will give details of its three \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the last two weeks, aimed at preventing a further weakening of the zloty that would feed into inflation.\par \par \uc2 "The elevated inflation, as well as a weak zloty speak against quick rate cuts," said Piotr Bielski, senior economist at \uc2 Bank Zachodni WBK\uc2 . "\b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the zloty and simultaneous rate cuts would be incoherent."\par \par \uc2 Annual price growth stood at 4.3 percent in August, still considerably above the bank's 2.5 percent target, after it reached a near-decade high of 5.0 percent in May.\par \par \uc2 After raising the key interest rate four times this year the MPC has adopted a wait-and-see approach since June to assess the impact of the tightening delivered so far on inflation.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the MPC to start cutting interest rates next year given the expected economic slowdown, with the timing of the first move depending, among other factors, on the zloty exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Marcin Goettig, writing by Chris Borowski; Editing by Catherine Evans)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-RATES/ (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111008e7a5000bb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
