\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Polish c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  again, to little effect\b0\par\par\uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2011\par 10:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Polish c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on mkt, fails to boost PLN\par \par \uc2  * Market players say amount was small\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could boost ECB fixing crucial for farm subsidies \par \par \uc2 (Adds more comments, background)\par \par \uc2  By Dagmara Leszkowicz\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Sept 30 (Reuters) - Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again on Friday a week after an unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the weakening zloty, hinting at a broader determination to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall.\par \par \uc2  The zloty has been on the front line of investors' retreat from emerging European assets as the global economy faces a potential new downturn and confidence fades over euro zone policymakers' ability to reverse a debt crisis.\par \par \uc2  While Polish authorities' move to firm the zloty last week sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up 3 percent against the euro, dealers said Friday's action was more muted and after an initial boost the impact on the zloty was minimal.\par \par \uc2  By 1440 GMT, the zloty was down 0.2 percent on the day to trade at 4.4241 to the euro. It a session high of 4.40 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  initially asked for prices from dealers.\par \par \uc2  Markets are testing the thresholds at which eastern European authorities will step in to bolster their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Polish bank's governor, Marek Belka, has warned of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to battle volatility.  \par \par \uc2  Analysts and dealers said the action on Friday was a further warning, but could also be more destabilising.\par \par \uc2  "It appears we've been underestimating the scope of the change in the NBP's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is starting to look like a more permanent feature in the (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) market," Mateusz Szczurek, chief economist for CEE at ING Bank, said in a client note.\par \par \uc2  REGULAR DEAL\par \par \uc2  Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also was seen in the market by dealers in Bucharest on Friday, while emerging market policymakers globally have actively tried to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the flight away from risk. \par \par \uc2  A weaker zloty puts pressures on households that have taken out popular foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans, while the weak exchange rate can also push government debt to near levels that might exceed a legally binding public debt ceiling and trigger spending cuts.\par \par \uc2  Even before the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month, \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has regularly converted EU funds on the market through state-owned bank BGK. The Finance Ministry said on Friday these \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  would depend on liquidity.\par \par \uc2   Dealers have said this week that markets were testing the added threat of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and some dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves would rather contribute to volatility. \par \par \uc2  The zloty touched as low as 4.4650 this week, putting it down 7 percent for September but still well shy of the 27-month low of 4.5370 it hit before the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has lost a cumulative 10.9 percent since July 1.\par \par \uc2  "Given the fact that the move failed to boost the zloty, it appears that if the bank wants to step in again, it needs to sell at least twice as much to succeed," said one Warsaw-based dealer.   \par \par \uc2  This week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been aimed at strengthing the zloty ahead of Friday's European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixing at 1215 GMT, crucial for calculation of European Union subsidies for farmers, some analysts said.\par \par \uc2  Poland should get some 3.4 billion euros in direct payments for farmers in 2011-2012, but the payout will be spread between December 2011 and June 2012, according to the Finance Ministry. \par \par \uc2 (Addidional reporting by Filip Kochan; Editing by Jason Hovet)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-ZLOTY/CBANK  (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111003e79u000jd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
