\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Hungarian Budget Talk, Czech Minutes In View\b0\par\par\uc2 By Leos Rousek   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 858 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2011\par 05:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par    Local/GMT \par  \par    0830/0630 Hungary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  2Q current account balance \par    0900/0700 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  minutes from Sep 22 policy meeting \par    1000/0800 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's August M2 money supply \par    1400/1200 Hungarian government officials at conference in Pecs \par    1400/1200 Poland's inflationary expectations in September \par       N/A    Poland to present debt issuance plans for 3Q \par       N/A    Hungary government submits '12 budget draft to parliament \par       N/A    EU's Eastern Partnership summit with post-Soviet states in Warsaw \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A conference featuring a number of Hungarian government officials, followed by minutes from the Sep. 22 rate-setting meeting by the Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely grab most headlines in the region Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 In Pecs, a town 230 kilometers south of Budapest, Hungary's government and debt management agency officials may share details on the government austerity budget plans for 2012, centered on spending cuts and higher taxation. The government wants to bring its budget deficit to maximum 2.5% of gross domestic product next year from 2.9% target for 2011.\par \par \uc2 In Prague, investors will peruse the minutes from the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Sep. 22 rate setting meeting at which two earlier hawks joined the five-member-strong dovish camp. All seven board members agreed to keep the base rate, the first unanimous votes since September 2010, unchanged at its all-time low of 0.75%.\par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Polish zloty and Hungarian forint may still face some selling pressure, while the koruna is likely to remain immune to any weakening.\par \par \uc2 The likely economic slowdown around the world may also weigh on the zloty, \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  said. The U.S. bank cut its estimate of Poland's economic growth for next year to 1.9% from 3.8% estimated for 2011.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par         Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                    2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par EUR/CZK 24.548-619 24.536-634  -0.01 24.566   24.594  -1.87 \par EUR/HUF 292.79-3.52 292.33-3.14 +0.14 293.18  292.88  +5.35 \par EUR/PLN 4.4295-380 4.4230-354 +0.10 4.4394   4.4304 +12.05 \par  \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par          Hungary        Poland          Czech Republic \par        Thu    Wed     Thu     Wed       Thu     Tue * \par 3 Yrs 6.95%  6.78%   4.46%   4.45%(1)  1.82%   1.82%(2) \par 5 yrs 7.45%  7.28%   5.24%   5.27%     2.00%   2.02% \par 10yrs 8.05%  7.88%   5.90%   5.89%     3.22%   3.20% \par (1) 2Yrs (2) 4Yrs (*) Czech markets were closed Wed \par  \par STOCKS \par EU Enlarged 15        1,739.10 gain 11.10 up 0.64% \par WIG 20                2,188.73 gain  7.14 up  0.33% \par BUX                  15,806.20 gain 193.67 up 1.24% \par PX                    941.3    gain   6.9  up  0.7% \par  \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Spain's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Santander SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (STD) is looking to buy something small in Poland to add to its bank there, Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alfredo Saenz\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: The Polish government may activate the $30 billion flexible credit line from the IMF if Greek debt restructuring is disorderly and the euro-zone crisis deepens, threatening contagion, says Nomura economic Peter Attard Montalto.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 POLAND\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : Polish state-owned Bank Gospodarstwa Krajowego Thursday was seen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets for the second time in less than a week to support the Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , one dealer with knowledge of the situation told Dow Jones Newswires.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: The Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , or CNB, Thursday said it will leave its market-liquidity-boosting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , centered on government bond buybacks, in place indefinitely despite low demand for the facility.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary has prepared a worst-case scenario budget for 2012, officials said Thursday, in response to forint volatility and a deteriorating economic outlook.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The budget, to be presented to the public Friday, is based on an lower economic growth forecast of 1.5% for next year, but the government must prepare for an even weaker outlook, said Mihaly Varga, state secretary of the prime minister's office.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: The European Commission and Hungary are set to go to court over a tax the country has imposed on its telecoms operators and that the Commission Thursday said was illegal.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Finnish cell-phone maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nokia\f28 \uc2 \f2  decided to shut down its plant in northwestern Romania, the manufacturer announced Thursday. The closure of the plant in Jucu, Cluj County, is estimated to affect about 2,200 employees, said a press release of the manufacturer, though the plant will stay open until the end of the year and employees will continue to receive wages until March 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Leos Rousek, Dow Jones Newswires; +420 222 315 290; leos.rousek@dowjones.com (Marcin Sobczyk in Warsaw and Veronika Gulyas in Budapest also contributed to this briefing.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe}}}\uc2 \f2  for the new Dow Jones blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 09-29-11 2306ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110930e79u0000g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
