\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 ,Slovak ECB Member Makuch In Focus\b0\par\par\uc2 By Leos Rousek   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 853 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2011\par 05:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par    Local/GMT \par  \par    1130/0930 Hungary three-month T-bill auction \par    1300/1100 Slovakia's ECB member Jozef Makuch press conference \par     all day  German president visits Slovakia \par      N/A     Polish government 2012 budget, debt strategy talks \par      N/A     European summit in Krakow on shale gas deposits \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors will remain focused on possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Polish and Hungarian central banks, while the Czech koruna market will remain a relative island of calm Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Investors in the Polish zloty are still digesting Friday's unexpected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the finance ministry to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to make investors less eager to bet that the zloty will weaken but that it will rather stabilize despite debt woes in Europe, Invest-Bank said.\par \par \uc2 "The koruna retains its safe harbor status for now," a Prague-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said.\par \par \uc2 Moreover the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the CNB, is seen as staying clear of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot market. "It seems to us that the only \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that will not be involved in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in CEE is the CNB," \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  said in a note to investors.\par \par \uc2 Events in Slovakia may get in the spotlight. They will center on the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy maker Jozef Makuch and his possible comments on the bank's rate policy plans and thoughts about offering 12-month refinancing securities to commercial banks.\par \par \uc2 Also in Bratislava, politicians from the senior coalition party SDKU may hold talks on whether Slovak lawmakers should liken the parliamentary vote on the European Financial Stability Facility salvage fund to a vote of confidence on the SDKU-led coalition itself. The government is split over the country's EFSF endorsement since junior coalition members, led by the parliamentary speaker Richard Sulik, refuse to support the euro rescue plan.\par \par \uc2 Without the votes of Sulik's team, Slovakia may be the only euro-zone country to hold up allowing the EFSF to prop up insolvent Greece.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par         Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                    2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par EUR/CZK 24.594-651  24.591-663  -0.02 24.610 24.644  -1.72 \par EUR/HUF 289.22-82   289.20-91  -0.13   290.07 289.78  +4.04 \par EUR/PLN 4.4073-120  4.4107-240  -0.17  4.4229 4.4066 +11.44 \par  \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par          Hungary        Poland          Czech Republic \par        Mon    Fri     Mon     Fri       Mon     Fri \par 3 Yrs 6.12%  6.83%   4.43%   4.49%(1)  1.74%   1.73%(2) \par 5 yrs 7.47%  7.50%   5.25%   5.25%     1.95%   1.92% \par 10yrs 7.75%  8.25%   5.95%   6.98%     3.17%   3.14% \par (1) 2Yrs (2) 4Yrs \par  \par STOCKS \par EU Enlarged 15       1,659.82 gain    13.16    up  0.80% \par WIG 20               2,115.22 gain     13.99   up  0.67% \par BUX                  14,929.80 loss   11.01    dn  0.07% \par PX                    901.7   gain     37.6    up  4.4% \par  \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 POLAND\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market last week will deter some investors from betting that the zloty will weaken, while stabilizing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the short term, economists said. The market may test the resolve of Polish authorities to defend the zloty if turmoil increases, they added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Poland's public debt will rise to 53.8% of economic output this year and fall to 51.7% in 2012, state-owned newswire PAP reports Monday, citing a government document.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fiat Auto Poland\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Polish unit of Italy's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fiat SpA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (F.MI), will lay off 435 people at its production plant in Tychy because of lower-than-anticipated car orders from outside Poland, the company's spokesman told Dow Jones Newswires Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: The Czech koruna is likely to lose its safe harbor status amid rough waters elsewhere in central and eastern Europe if western economies slow down, a former advisor to the country's finance minister said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: A free trade agreement between the European Union and Ukraine could boost Hungary's exports to the non-EU member, Foreign Minister Janos Martonyi said after talks in Brussels on Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Planned changes in Hungary's personal income tax regime won't affect next year's budget deficit target, which the government is committed to, the Economy Ministry told Dow Jones Newswires Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Romania's consolidated budget posted a deficit of 12.97 billion lei ($4.05 billion) in the first eight months, equal to 2.4% of the gross domestic product, Finance Ministry data showed Monday, news agency Mediafax reports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Leos Rousek, Dow Jones Newswires; +420 222 315 290; leos.rousek@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Marcin Sobczyk in Warsaw and Veronika Gulyas in Budapest also contributed to this briefing.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe}}}\uc2 \f2  for the new Dow Jones blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 27-09-11 0307GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110927e79r0006i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
