\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ NBP's Belka: We Can  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  On  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt Whenever We Wish To\b0\par\par\uc2 1,232 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2011\par 05:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT *DJ  NBP's Belka: We Can \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  On \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Mkt Whenever We Wish To\par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT *DJ  NBP's Belka: Doesn't Rule Out Further Market \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  To Support Zloty\par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT *DJ  NBP's Belka: \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Prompted By Signs Of Destabilization In \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Mkt\par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT *DJ  NBP's Belka: \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Showed Investors They Can Get Burnt\par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT *DJ  NBP's Belka: Talk Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Threshold To Contain Debt Is 'Nonsense'\par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT *DJ  NBP Governor Belka: Euro Crisis Would Jeopardize EU Future\par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT *DJ  NBP's Belka: Welcomes Idea Of Boosting EFSF Size To Meet July 21 Targets\par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT *DJ  NBP's Belka: There's Sense That IMF Should Be More Involved In EU Crisis\par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT *DJ  NBP's Belka: Global Slowdown Will Impact Poland, But Econ Seems Resilient\par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT *DJ  NBP's Belka: 'Unreasonable' To Move Either Way On Rates Now\par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT *DJ  NBP's Belka: Not Comfortable With Current Inflation Rate\par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT *DJ  NBP's Belka: Can't Follow Markets, They Are Too Volatile\par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT *DJ  NBP's Belka: Our Planning Horizon Much Longer Than Mkts\par \par \uc2 25 Sep 2011 23:59 EDT DJ  INTERVIEW:NBP's Belka: Not Targeting, Defending Any Level For Zloty\par \par \uc2 --NBP's Belka: Doesn't Rule Out Down Speculation Vs Zloty\par \par \uc2 --NBP's Belka: EU Needs IMF's Strong Conditionality Approach\par \par \uc2 --NBP's Belka: EU Needs More Self Confidence, Must Win Back Mkt Trust \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Gabriele Parussini \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets whenever it sees excessive volatility, but won't defend a set exchange rate for the zloty, Marek Belka, its governor, said Sunday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "What has been bothering us is what we call the destabilization of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, and we saw some signs of it. We can \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when we wish to and we can stop \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when we wish to," he told Dow Jones on the sidelines of the International Monetary Fund/World Bank semi-annual meeting. "We didn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to defend any levels; we \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because it was going in a disorderly way, too far too fast, and - to a certain extent - without a reason."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Belka warned, may repeat its surprise action.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If we think that the situation becomes worrying or something strange is happening on the market then we may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Belka's comments came two days after the Polish government and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  propped up the zloty, which had been weakening since July, as investors exited emerging markets over euro-zone sovereign debt concerns and worries about the global economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose nearly 3% against the euro in less than 30 minutes Friday afternoon, back to Wednesday levels, which were still about 6% below the exchange rate of September 1.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday's move served to punish speculators who had been betting against the zloty, Belka said, but investors shouldn't read too much into it.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I can't rule out that some people were speculating against the zloty. We would like to highlight to the people that it's a two-way street. You can burn your fingers, you have to take into account an additional risk factor in your trades: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said. "It was a random \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Don't read any trend in this."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market has wide-ranging implications for Poland. A weak zloty inflates the country's debts denominated in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Before the zloty began weakening, Poland's public debt was around 53% of gross domestic product, well below the European Union average, but as its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  falls, the country's debt swells. And if the debt-to-GDP ratio crosses the crucial 55% threshold at the end of the year, Polish law requires the government to balance the budget or have a surplus.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And estimations on what's the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level that will push the country's debt over the threshold vary--around PLN4.66, according to BRE Bank, PLN4.7, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But Belka denied he's paying much attention to that.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "All this talk about thresholds on public debt to GDP is just nonsense. This is nothing that really is of major concern to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 ministry of finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or to us," he said. "We don't even know what this crucial exchange rate is. It changes every day."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Belka, who faces a tough rate-setting balancing act, juggling slowing economic growth and inflation--at 4.3% in August, well above the NBP's 2.5% target--ruled out swift interest rate moves, and said the 4.5% key rate, which has been hiked 100 basis points in the first half of this year, is unlikely to move any time soon.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In such an unstable world it's probably quite reasonable to stay put and not to exclude any option either up or down with interest rates," he said. "There is always this call to be ahead of the curve. But in the case of a country like Poland the problem is that the curve is so curvy, so to say, that it is probably better to at least project some stability and continuity on the economy than to try and change gears hectically every now and then as the markets prompt us to."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We should not follow the markets because they change opinion so fast," Belka said. "I think a good point is to be "behind the curve". Let the markets look at us and follow us. Our planning horizon is much longer than theirs."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Looking outside of the country's borders, the governor expressed preoccupation for the euro zone, arguing that a crisis of the euro as a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would put in doubt the whole European project, and backed the idea of boosting the resources of the European Financial Stability Facility, or EFSF, to increase its firepower in the event of a crisis, an idea that was one of the main talking points behind the scenes at the IMF meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He also said that talks surfaced of a wider involvement of the IMF in the solution of the European sovereign debt crisis, but then ultimately the only thing that could take markets back to normal would be a confidence boost.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "What Europe needs is the confidence of the markets, as well as the confidence in its own capabilities to solve this crisis," he said, although the issuance of euro zone bonds, which some see as the most radical remedy to solve the crisis, would be an ineffective shortcut before a deeper integration were realized within the euro zone. "It's more or less a political crisis these days."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But high market volatility and investors' hysteria remain the governor's top concerns.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We're not talking about rational investors anymore," he said. "This is a nuthouse."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Gabriele Parussini, Dow Jones Newswires; gabriele.parussini@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 25, 2011 23:59 ET (03:59 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110926e79q000i7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
