 levels in the tailings pond of a future Romanian gold mine would cost "several dozen million dollars," a manager of the Canadian company seeking to exploit it told AFP. Rosia Montana Gold Corp., which is 80% held by Canadian firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gabriel Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (GBU.T), wants to use cyanide to extract 300 metric tons of gold from an open-cast mine in Rosia Montana, a picturesque Carpathian mountain village.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BULGARIA: Bulgaria threatened Saturday to make European Union decision-making more difficult after having its entry into the passport-free Schengen travel area blocked.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Leos Rousek, Dow Jones Newswires; +420 222 315 290; leos.rousek@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe}}}\uc2 \f2  for the new Dow Jones blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 26-09-11 0312GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020110926e79q00004\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
