\par\par \b \uc2 Poland c.bank head: ready to aid banks with liquidity\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lidia Kelly   \par \uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2011\par 09:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Sept 25 (Reuters) - Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to supply the country's banking system with liquidity if a need arises and its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be random, Governor Marek Belka said late on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 The current storms in the European economy carry a risk of shortages of available cash, Belka told journalists at the sidelines of the International Monetary Fund/World Bank autumn meeting in Washington.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to, if it becomes necessary, to supply liquidity to Polish banks," he said.\par \par \uc2 "They should feel secure. Even if the international banking system dries up they can count on us."\par \par \uc2 Belka also said that should the current destabilisation in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market continue, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will carry out intermittent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at keeping the rouble from sliding and spooking speculative investors.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Polish authorities launched an unprecedented coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt markets to rescue the zloty and bonds, which have been pummelled this week by the global flight from risk.\par \par \uc2 The move drove up the zloty more than two percent against the euro.\par \par \uc2 "We will be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  - randomly, when we will decide that the market is destabilizing, but not defending any rate," Belka said.\par \par \uc2 Friday's move was the bank's first \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since April 9, 2010, and only the second since \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  adopted its free-float system for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The zloty had tested 27-month lows against the euro in recent days amid fears of a second global recession and the debt crisis in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 The governor also said that the government has been doing a good job on lowering budget deficit and will have no problem of reaching this year's target of 5.6 percent of gross domestic product (GDP).\par \par \uc2 "In general I think we will be nicely surprised with our fiscal results this year," Belka said. "Maybe the same will happen next year. Here, we are not that confident."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Lidia Kelly; Editing by Ed Lane)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-BELKA/BANKS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110928e79p000a5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
