\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Wars Metamorphose Amid Dollar Scramble\b0\par\par\uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2011\par 17:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Emerging markets prop up plummeting \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , having previously tried to cap strength\par \par \uc2 --Central banks in Asia, Brazil, Poland and Russia take action\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Clare Connaghan \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--So much for the global battle to hold \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down to keep a competitive edge. Now authorities around the world are \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop them up in the wake of a mad scramble for dollars, especially in export-orientated Asia.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Friday, the National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the flagging zloty, after the Bank of Korea, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Russia were all suspected of stepping in to support the won, rupee and ruble, respectively. That follows a week in which central banks across the developing world bought their local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect them from the biggest sell-off in emerging market assets since the demise of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lehman Brothers\f28 \uc2 \f2  three years ago.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even Brazil, which until recently was battling hard to cap an appreciating real, was forced to take action after the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  racked up losses in excess of 10% in the space of just four trading days.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As a result, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wars of the recent past have metamorphosed, with authorities in emerging markets this time having to embark on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -strengthening programs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This is about trying to contain emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation pressures," said Benoit Anne, head of emerging market strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London. "What we have seen over the past few days is a number of central banks stepping in, with a view to smoothing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility," he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With investors scrambling to unwind non-core trading positions and switch into dollars due to a toxic combination of weakening global economic data and escalating euro-zone debt worries, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia, Latin America, Eastern Europe and Africa have come under intense selling pressure.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sudden \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness can pose inflationary problems, by lifting the cost of imported goods, and for those countries burdened with large amounts of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -denominated debt, it's particularly harmful as these debts become much more expensive to pay back.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 So central banks in Asia, especially, are suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this week to defend their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , including those in South Korea, Indonesia, Thailand, India, the Philippines, Singapore and Taiwan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Many [Asian] central banks have a policy of maintaining low volatility in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, which meant over the past year it prevented \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation, but now it's the other way round," said Ilan Solot of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brown Brothers Harriman\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also stepped in to sell $2.7 billion in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap contracts Thursday to rein in the depreciating real, while Russia is thought to have sold about $2 billion Friday to support the ruble.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Clare Connaghan, Dow Jones Newswires, +44 (0) 20 7842 9496;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 clare.connaghan@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (William Kemble-Diaz contributed to this article.) [ 23-09-11 1549GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 5008   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110923e79n0010i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
