\par\par \b \uc2 Polish finance ministry pleased by c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 132 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2011\par 16:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Sept 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry welcomes Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Polish zloty, Deputy Finance Minister Dominik Radzwill told Reuters in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it had sold "a certain amount" of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for zlotys, confirming earlier reports from dealers and sending the zloty up some 2 percent versus the euro since Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2 "The (current) market situation justifies selling a larger amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at an favourable rate," Radziwill said. "We are cooperating with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and welcome today's decision by the National Bank of Poland."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Pawel Sobczak, writing by Gabriela Baczynska; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 POLISH-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FINMIN (URGENT)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110926e79n0011w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
