\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervenes \highlight\uc2  to rescue zloty, bonds\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dagmara Leszkowicz and Pawel Sobczak   \par \uc2 436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2011\par 15:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Combines takes, adds reaction)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Sept 23 (Reuters) - Polish authorities launched an unprecedented coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt markets on Friday to rescue the zloty and bonds, which have been pummelled this week by the global flight from risk.\par \par \uc2 The moved marked another strike on markets by an emerging economy on Friday, after South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the won and Indian authorities hauled up the rupee.\par \par \uc2 The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement it had sold "a certain amount of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 " for zlotys, confirming earlier reports from dealers. The move drove up the zloty\par \par \uc2 more than two percent against the euro.\par \par \uc2 "This is an unprecedented situation, and they clearly hit the target as amounts were not that big and it worked," said a Warsaw-based fixed-income dealer.\par \par \uc2 The dealers also said the state-owned BGK bank, which acts on behalf of the finance ministry, had bought bonds on the secondary market in a move that sent yields on longer-dated papers 10 basis points lower.\par \par \uc2 The BGK declined to comment on the reports.\par \par \uc2 "The (current) market situation justifies selling a larger amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a favourable rate," Deputy Finance Minister Dominik Radziwill told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 "We are cooperating with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and welcome today's decision by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move was the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at supporting the zloty since April 9, 2010 and only the second since Poland adopted its free-float system for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The zloty has tested 27-month lows against the euro in recent days amid fears of a second global recession and the debt crisis in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 At 1427 GMT it traded at 4.398 to the euro, up 2.8 percent from Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the zloty may firm further in coming days following the authorities' \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which also helped the Warsaw bourse to pare some of its losses.\par \par \uc2 "The bank wants to limit the volatility of the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . High volatility is bad both for the financial system and companies," said Piotr Bielski, an economist at BZ WBK Bank in Warsaw.\par \par \uc2 "There is no guarantee that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be successful because we have a lot of uncertainty about the direction of the global economy. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to show the market that it doesn't pay to overreact to global uncertainty."\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Gareth Jones; Editing by Toby Chopra)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 POLAND\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2   (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110926e79n0010j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
