\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-INTERVIEW-Poland to use BGK bank to support debt mkt\b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2011\par 16:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Finance ministry says ready to back fixed income market\par \par \uc2 * State-owned BGK bank could buy bonds in case of turmoil\par \par \uc2 By Dagmara Leszkowicz and Pawel Sobczak\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, April 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has mandated state-owned bank BGK to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the bond market to soothe potential tensions, the head of the finance ministry's debt department said in comments authorised for release on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Polish authorities already used BGK at the end of 2010 to sell euros in order to keep the zloty strong and avoid breaching key debt levels. [ID:nLDE6AN140]\par \par \uc2 "We see the possibility of using BGK to support the bond market in case of tensions unrelated to fundamentals," Piotr Marczak told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 "BGK would be able to buy bonds on the secondary market. We (the finance ministry) could guarantee to buy back these papers if need be."\par \par \uc2 The ministry does not rule out running fully transparent debt buy-back auctions, he said.\par \par \uc2 "Running a buy-back auction requires some time and making declarations of what and how much you want to buy. If we work through BGK we have flexibility both in terms of time, the type of bonds and the sums involved," Marczak said.\par \par \uc2 Just as with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ministry will not inform investors when BGK intends to buy bonds from the market but will say when it buys back bonds from BGK, he said.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors currently hold Polish treasuries worth over 140 billion zlotys ($51.04 billion) and both the ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must keep reserves to protect against potential capital flight in the case of a major crisis.\par \par \uc2 The ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would work hand in hand to calm the market in the event of a "large" crisis, Marczak said.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting: Marcin Goettig; writing by Maciej Onoszko)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-BONDS/ (UPDATE 1, INTERVIEW)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110411e748001a4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
