\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2  To Boost PLN 'With Rates,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 '\b0\par\par\uc2 1,100 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2011\par 12:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London: +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1110 GMT (Dow Jones) The Polish government and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will succeed in strengthening the zloty through raising rates and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , if needed, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Polish bond yields will shift up across the curve on global market trends and domestic policy. Polish growth may be under pressure due to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthening coupled with fiscal and monetary tightening, all working against growth goals, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1106 GMT (Dow Jones) EUR/USD slides to the day's low of 1.3610 after uncertainty arises over just who will take over from Jean-Claude Trichet as president of the ECB now that Bundesbank President and red hot favorite Axel Weber seems to be out of the frame. EUR/USD had been trading around 1.3650 before headlines hit the wires. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1106 GMT (Dow Jones) The dollar is steady mid-morning in European trading Wednesday ahead of Federal Reserve chairman Ben Bernanke's testimony to the House Budget Committee on the economy from 1500 GMT. A sharp rally in U.S. yields is boosting the dollar against the safe-haven yen and Swiss franc, while the greenback gains back some ground against the euro ahead of Bernanke's testimony. EUR/USD is down at 1.3632, USD/JPY is up at 82.56, while GBP/USD is little changed at 1.6089. (clare.connaghan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1104 GMT (Dow Jones) EUR/USD sheds 40 ticks to the day's low of 1.3612, following a news report by Reuters suggesting that Bundesbank chief Weber will not be a candidate to replace Trichet as president of the ECB. The Bundesbank declined to comment. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1103 GMT (Dow Jones) EUR/HUF looks well supported around the 270 area, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBC Capital Markets\f28 \uc2 \f2 . High interest rates, the promise of fiscal reform and a low headline fiscal deficit should keep the EUR/HUF near 270, it adds. RBC expects Hungary's policy rate to remain at its current level of 6.00% for the rest of the year, even though the four new members to enter the Monetary Policy Council in March could out vote the three remaining MPC members. Hungary's economic recovery will take longer given the fiscal restraints. 2011 GDP growth is seen at 3% and CPI at 4.5%. EUR/HUF is at 270.90. (margit.feher@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1101 GMT (Dow Jones) Polish bond yields have limited room upward unless negative newsflow keeps coming to the market regularly, says BRE Bank. It adds that CPI risks are already priced in and yields should stabilize at current levels. The spread between Polish and Hungarian 10-year bonds is at its lowest in 12 months and a reversal of the trend is likely, especially for longer maturities, BRE says, advising to go long on Polish bonds. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1100 GMT (Dow Jones) EUR/AUD is looking in good shape Wednesday, trading close to a one-week high of 1.3510. Immediate resistance is Fibonacci around 1.3515, which is a 38.2% retracement of the early-January to late-January decline. After that, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  has a target of 1.3638 and then the January highs of 1.3880. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1059 GMT (Dow Jones) The expected path of monetary tightening shows the market expects Polish CPI to rise to 4.3% in the coming quarters, says BRE Bank. CPI will rise on higher taxes and prices of raw materials outside the country. Monetary tightening on the scale the market expects isn't likely, BRE adds. Poland's CPI was 3.1% on the year in December.(marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1055 GMT [Dow Jones] There's more activity in the short-end of the German curve with the 2-year schatz still weak after yields rose by 9 bps Tuesday. The 2-year schatz is currently yielding 1.45% while the schatz future currently trades at 107.945. There's also been reasonable activity seen in the options space with the April 106.90/107.30 put spread being bought vs selling the April 107.90 calls. (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1055 GMT (Dow Jones) PLN weakens after Polish central banker Kazmierczak said Polish 10-year bond yields may hit 7% and send the country close to default. However, the weakness can be seen across the region, mainly due to low Czech inflation numbers and a long USD/TRY recommendation from a major bank, says Nigel Rendell, an emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at RBC in London. He adds that the central banker is likely trying to encourage the Polish government to sort out the country's fiscal situation. EUR/PLN currently at 3.9014, from 3.89 at the start of London trading. (eva.szalay@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1050 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds are slightly higher as bargain hunters find elevated yields attractive and bet on easing food inflation, with data due Thursday, and lower factory output numbers, due Friday, says a senior dealer at a state-run bank. The 8.13% 2022 bond is at 99.30 from 99.25 late Tuesday. "We also don't expect the government to auction the INR100 billion worth of securities it had cut in the previous quarter, which is also supporting bond prices," the dealer says. He tips the 8.13% 2022 yield to trade in a 8.20%-8.25% band in the near term from 8.22% last quoted and 8.23% last close. (sourav.mishra@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1048 GMT (Dow Jones) Fed Chairman Bernanke will appear at the House Budget Committee at 1500 GMT and \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  is looking for a dovish statement. The bank expects Bernanke to reiterate his view that whilst the recovery is strong, it is not strong enough to bring employment down to an acceptable level while on QE, he is expected to reiterate the need to continue the program with no hints of an extension after June. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 02-09-11 0610ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110209e7290007q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
