\par\par \b \uc2 Zloty Hits Highest Level Since April 2010  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Marynia Kruk   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2011\par 12:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The zloty hit a nine-month high against the euro Wednesday and closed in on the level it reached last April when the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The zloty has been supported by expectations of rate increases. Over the past two weeks, comments by members of Poland's Monetary Policy Council, most recently Jan Winiecki speaking today on TVN CNBC, have convinced investors that the council will begin a sequence of interest rate hikes in January to counter rising inflation.\par \par \uc2 As recently as December, most economists thought the council would hold fire on Jan. 19 but that is slowly changing. At 1047 GMT, the zloty was at PLN3.8419 to the euro from PLN3.9693 Dec. 23.\par \par \uc2 "The zloty is supported by council member comments," said Piotr Kalisz, an economist at Citi in Warsaw.\par \par \uc2 Andrzej Bratkowski, another member of the 10-person council commented in detail on the outlook for the zloty on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "The zloty could gain through 2011 even to 3.5 [versus the euro] at the end of the year," Bratkowski said. "Such a level could actually slow economic growth down slightly, but it would not pose any bigger threat."\par \par \uc2 He added that 3.70-3.80 would be an "optimal" level for the euro-zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair.\par \par \uc2 The fact that Bratkowski emphasized 3.50 as a goal for the EUR/PLN was very significant for markets, Kalisz at Citi said.\par \par \uc2 Winiecki said that although Poland is doing well, inflation is rising and that the rate setting council needs to reflect this in its decisions.\par \par \uc2 On April 9, a day before Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief as well as the country's president died in a plane crash in Russia that also killed dozens of other officials, Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought an undisclosed amount of euros at PLN3.8450-PLN3.8500, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Then, over the following nine months, the zloty's volatility versus the euro moderated. The EUR/PLN broadly fluctuated in a 4.10-3.90 range until the end of 2010.\par \par \uc2 -By Marynia Kruk, Dow Jones Newswires; +48 22 447-2431; marynia.kruk@dowjones.com [ 12-01-11 1130GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110112e71c000xb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
