\par\par \b \uc2 Polish Central Banker Hints At  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  - Report\b0\par\par\uc2 143 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2010\par 08:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's presence on the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market should be considered with the aim of limiting the volatility of the zloty, a Polish central banker is quoted as saying by state-owned news agency PAP.\par \par \uc2 "I'm of the opinion that the presence of the NBP on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is worth considering to limit high volatility of the zloty," said Witold Kozinski, deputy governor of the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The zloty has remained in the range of approximately 3.88-4.02 zlotys to the euro since August. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April, when the zloty was 3.85 to the euro, to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Agency website: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.pap.pl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.pap.pl}}}\par \par \uc2 -Warsaw Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; +48 22 447 2432 [ 18-11-10 0738GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101118e6bi000hk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
