\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Polish Bonds Weaken After Sep CPI Jump\b0\par\par\uc2 1,233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2010\par 16:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1400 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish treasury bonds weaken following higher-than-expected September CPI, to +2.5% from +2.0% in August. But traders expect the bonds to bounce back on Thursday as the market starts to realize rate hike in October is still unlikely. Average yield on 2-year bonds is at 4.73% from 4.59% late Tuesday, 5-year at 5.14% from 5.04%, and 10-year at 5.52% from 5.44%. EUR/PLN is at 3.9484 from 3.9512 earlier Wednesday, USD/PLN at 2.8331 from 2.8259. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1354 GMT [Dow Jones] Investors are often obsessed by round numbers in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and there is much discussion about AUD and CAD breaking parity, says CitiFx. "We see this obsession as misplaced since both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are largely driven by global asset market and economic conditions," it says. "Bigger surprise" will be how fast parity broken under the right scenario. The "right conditions" are a continuation of the equity and commodities rally and continued USD pressure, Citi says. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1352 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds fall Wednesday, weighed by hawkish comments from ECB governing council member Weber overnight and buoyant stocks. Weber said the risks from "exiting too late" from its easy monetary stance outweighed those from "exiting too early," adding it was necessary not to defer ending non-standard measures for too long. His comments appear in sharp contrast to the Fed stance, with FOMC minutes on Tuesday hinting that quantitative easing looked increasingly likely in November. "The ECB its clearly getting the message across that it is keen to withdraw non-standard liquidity \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Money market rates are expected to keep drifting higher," says a London-based trader. Earlier Wednesday, Germany sold 10-year bunds at the lowest yield ever while euro zone industrial output grew a little more than forecast. December bunds are down 0.41 at 131.60 and the 10-year bund is down at 99.80 to yield 2.273%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1351 GMT [Dow Jones] Traditional asset-allocation trades are back in style for now, featuring inverse relationship of higher stock prices and lower Tsys. "We are struck by the equity market's ability to push higher on the prospects of further [Fed] accommodation while the upside in Tsy [prices] appears to be growing tired," says David Ader, head of government bond market strategy for CRT Capital Group. Ader suggests fatigue is setting in because the market is tired of pricing in an "unknown" amount of quantitative easing. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1349 GMT [Dow Jones] Emerging market bonds are stronger as stocks get a boost on solid earnings. Sentiment also strengthened after FOMC minutes a day earlier indicated the likelihood of more stimulus. China's trade data is also supporting confidence. The risk premium on \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's Emerging Markets Bond Index Global is 12 bps tighter to 277 bps over Tsys. The index is up 0.33%. Brazil's benchmark bond, the Global 2040, is up 5/16 to 140 3/4 bid, according to Reuters. (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1335 GMT [Dow Jones] As the yen continues to appreciate, analysts expect another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At next week's G7 meeting, Japan will try to achieve a formal permission slip for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says Adam Kritzer at forexblog.org, by arguing "'Our \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't the kind of large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  that aim to achieve certain rate levels over the long term.' September's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was only 'aimed at curbing excess fluctuations' in the yen's rates." Depending on how the G7 responds (via its official statement), it may influence the likelihood of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (darlene.ross@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.forexblog.org/2010/10/japan-plots-next-yen-intervention.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.forexblog.org/2010/10/japan-plots-next-yen-\b  \highlight22intervention\b0 \highlight22 .html}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 1334 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's higher-than-expected September inflation rate cements expectations that the country's Monetary Policy Council will raise interest rates by 25 basis points at its October meeting, \uc2 Bank BPH\uc2  says. Inflation hitting the middle of the council's inflation target lends credence to the members of the council who have been calling for an increase for some time. Food prices are key determinants of inflation expectations. As they were a big contributor to September inflation, it gives the council an additional reason to raise rates. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1334 GMT [Dow Jones] Market speculation and subsequent reports that Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have moved the ruble trading band, where it allows free fluctuations, are "not reliable" in the absence of official comment, Renaissance Capital says. The ruble weakened quite a bit against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-euro trading band before recovering to close official trade Wednesday at 35.4798, compared with 35.3098 late Tuesday. Previous reports suggested the trading band was between about 34.35 and 35.35 to the basket. If the band mov