\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stocks fall 1 pct, zloty hits 3-mth high\b0\par\par\uc2 632 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2010\par 12:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Emerging stocks drop 1 pct, but debt spreads tighten\par \par \uc2 * Zloty at 3-mth high, Polish c.bank warns against uptrend\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine 5-yr CDS trade around 500 bps after rate cut\par \par \uc2 By Carolyn Cohn\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Aug 10 (Reuters) - Emerging stocks fell 1 percent to an eight-day low on Tuesday, as caution about Federal Reserve policy dented risky assets, but the Polish zloty hit fresh three-month highs, prompting a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warning.\par \par \uc2 Emerging assets have had a good run in the last few weeks, boosted by the easing of the euro zone sovereign debt crisis and a refocus on strong domestic fundamentals. However, speculation has been growing that the U.S. Federal Reserve will at its meeting later on Tuesday signal a need for more stimulus to support U.S. growth or possibly restart asset purchases, known as quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 Chinese stocks <.SSEC> also fell 2.9 percent after weak import data spurred concerns domestic demand was cooling faster than previously thought. "Everywhere is down today, reflecting a general pullback in risk appetite which is hitting emerging markets," said Neil Shearing, senior emerging markets economist at Capital Economics.\par \par \uc2 The MSCI emerging equities index <.MSCIEF> dropped 1 percent to an eight-day low and the Thomson Reuters Emerging Europe index <.TRXFLDEEPU> fell 0.77 percent.\par \par \uc2 Emerging sovereign debt spreads tightened by 2 basis points to 261 bps over U.S. Treasuries <11EMJ>, however, and are trading around their narrowest in three months in the absence of new supply over the quiet August period.\par \par \uc2 The South African rand eased from 2-1/2 year highs against the dollar <ZAR=> set on Monday, as public sector unions threatened a prolonged strike. [ID:nWEB4785] As the zloty hit a fresh three-month high against the euro close to 3.95 <EURPLN=>, Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Marek Belka said he hoped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation trend would not be too strong. [ID:nLDE67905R]\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been volatile in recent months and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  both to buy and sell zloty.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to hike interest rates as soon as Q4 this year," said analysts at ING in a client note.\par \par \uc2 "Should this expectation build, euro/zloty may well re-test its April (3.80) mark."\par \par \uc2 Debt insurance costs climbed slightly in emerging Europe. Ukraine's five-year CDS rose to 505.4 bps, according to CMA DataVision, after dipping to a four-month low below 500 bps on Monday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its key discount rate by 75 basis points to 7.75 percent, the third cut this year.\par \par \uc2 Analysts see inflationary pressures in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation will go up," said Shearing. "We will see the effect from the gas price rise and there is the food angle too."\par \par \uc2 Ukraine raised domestic gas prices this month and traders say the drought-hit country is holding up wheat exports. [ID:nLDE6781NO]\par \par \uc2 Russian 5-year CDS also ticked up as oil prices weakened and investors focused on the smog in Moscow and the drought, which prompted Russia last week to ban grain exports.\par \par \uc2 "The drought will have an impact on the Russian economy and inflation and food prices in particular, and I wouldn't want to underplay that. But comparisons with the food price shocks of 2007-2008 are misplaced," said Shearing.\par \par \uc2 "Part of the problem back then was that the Russian economy was operating above potential but now it is operating below potential and it's difficult to see the food price inflation leading to wage inflation and feeding through massively into core inflation." (Additional reporting by Sujata Rao; Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|PX|HX|CZS|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100813e68a000sj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
