\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2  does not need  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\uc2  -c.banker\b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 2010\par 10:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, June 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not need \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the zloty but the exchange rate is key for monetary policy, a member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council (MPC) said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "I don't see any signals coming from inflation, from wage pressures to change monetary policy," Jerzy Hausner told a seminar.\par \par \uc2 "The zloty exchange rate is key and any signal to change monetary policy would come frome here."\par \par \uc2 The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has see-sawed with choppy global financial markets in recent months, and markets have been watching official comments on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closely after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter zloty strength.\par \par \uc2 There were also reports in May that the finance ministry had sold euros on the market, something it can do periodically with EU and other inflows to influence the zloty.\par \par \uc2 Several \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, including new governor Marek Belka, have said they expect the zloty to gain steadily over the longer term against the euro. Belka said last week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not target any particular zloty level.\par \par \uc2 Hausner said that while a steady strengthening of the zloty would not be a cause for concern, a rapid appreciation would be.\par \par \uc2 "Hausner's comments fit the view of the newly appointed bank's governor Marek Belka," said Jakub Wiraszka, a dealer at BRE bank in Warsaw.\par \par \uc2 The zloty <EURPLN=> was almost unchanged at 4.0660 to the euro in morning trade. Hausner also expressed concern about Poland's high general government budget deficit, saying that if it remained near 7 percent in 2011, that would be a reason to raise interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The budget deficit is expected to reach 6.9 percent of gross domestic output this year due to the economic slowdown, which has battered tax revenues.\par \par \uc2 The centre-right government sees the deficit easing to 5.9 percent of GDP next year and to 2.9 percent in 2012, below the EU's 3 percent ceiling, though some analysts are sceptical that it can fall that fast.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main interest rate is currently at a historic low of 3.5 percent. Analysts expect the bank to start hiking rates later this year as the recovery gathers pace. (Reporting by Pawel Sobczak, Writing by Dagmara Leszkowicz and Chris Borowski; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-ZLOTY/CBANKER (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|PX|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100616e66g000ec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
