\par\par \b \uc2 Poland - Factors to Watch on May 21\b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2010\par 08:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  WARSAW, May 21 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Poland's financial markets on Friday. ALL TIMES GMT (Poland GMT + 2 hours):\par \par \uc2  DATA\par \par \uc2  Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  releases net inflation data <PLNINF=ECI> for April at 1200 GMT. Analysts polled by Reuters expect the figure to come in at 1.8 percent on an annual basis.\par \par \uc2  TBILLS\par \par \uc2  Poland's finance ministry releases at 1000 GMT the details of its 48-week treasury bills tender due on Monday.\par \par \uc2  KOMOROWSKI ON NEW C.BANK HEAD\par \par \uc2  Poland's Acting President Bronislaw Komorowski told a radio broadcast he would present the parliament with a candidate for the new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governor before the June 20 election only if there was a guarantee the majority of MPs would support the candidate.\par \par \uc2  Komorowski said it would be better for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have the new chief installed promptly, but that he was not willing to risk loosing a good candidacy in the vote during election campaign.\par \par \uc2  FIN MIN ON CRISIS\par \par \uc2  Further turbulence on global markets cannot be ruled out later in the year and Poland's new president must support the government's reforms, Poland's Finance Minister Jacek Rostowski told daily Polska The Times in an interview. \par \par \uc2  POLAND AND EURO\par \par \uc2  Poland should still join the euro zone, though it will take a few years before the country is ready to do so and the zone itself overcomes its current problems, the IMF's head for Europe, Marek Belka, told daily Dziennik Gazeta Prawna in an interview.\par \par \uc2  ZLOTY\par \par \uc2  Dealers reported \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government on Thursday, pointing to sales of euros by a state-owned bank as an official attempt to control the zloty's sharp slide. [nLDE64J1NN]\par \par \uc2  NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming events see [PL/DIARY] and a calendar of east European economic indicators see [CONV/DIARY].\par \par \uc2    For other related news, double click on: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Polish equities       [PL-E]     E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  Polish money          [PL-M]     Polish debt           [PL-D]\par  Eastern Europe        [EEU]      All emerging markets  [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks            [HOT]      Stock markets         [STX]\par  Market debt news      [DBT]      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news            [FRX]\par  \par  For real-time index quotes, double click on:\par  Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20>  Budapest BUX <.BUX>  Prague PX <.PX>\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  ($1=3.331 Zloty)\f28 \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|PX|RBN|REVU|E|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100521e65l000cz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
