\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW-Polish c.bank keeps key rate flat, as expected\b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2010\par 12:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, April 28 (Reuters) - Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its main interest rate <PLINTR=ECI> unchanged on Wednesday, in line with market expectations that it would hold fire as inflation is easing and uncertainty over the pace of recovery remains high.\par \par \uc2 The main rate remains at a record low of 3.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 The bank will hold a news conference and release a statement explaining its decision at 1300 GMT.\par \par \uc2 *************************************************************\par \par \uc2 FORECAST\par \par \uc2 * All 26 analysts polled by Reuters earlier in April expected the Monetary Policy Council's (MPC) 10 members to keep the main interest rate at its all-time low of 3.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 MARKET REACTION\par \par \uc2 * The Polish zloty <EURPLN=D3> <PLN=> and bonds were unchanged immediately after the decision.\par \par \uc2 ANALYSTS' COMMENTS:\par \par \uc2 MARCIN MROWIEC, CHIEF ECONOMIST AT PEKAO BANK:\par \par \uc2 "This isn't a surprise. At the earliest, rates may be increased in the second half of the year, and most probably in the fourth quarter. At the same time we'd like to point out that they don't need to be raised at all.\par \par \uc2 "Looking at the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the fact that inflation will be low, while economic growth below its potential, the situation (of no hikes) is becoming more and more probable."\par \par \uc2 "What is more, the MPC discussed the possibility of rate cuts. So the probability of no rate hikes is rising and today's decision fits this scenario."\par \par \uc2 "We expect the next two or three rate sittings to be the same."\par \par \uc2 RAFAL BENECKI, SENIOR ECONOMIST AT ING BANK:\par \par \uc2 "We expect rather marginal changes in the statement due to the fact that some of the improvement on the labour market, construction and retail sales is a seasonal phenomenon (the recovery of economic activity after a tough winter). A hawkish statement would also be inconsistent with the MPC's attempts to slow the appreciation, though the importance of this factor recently diminished as lower risk appetite externally diminished the appreciation pressure.\par \par \uc2 "Economic growth still strongly depends on exports, while domestic demand will remain in the back seat this year. CPI is still decreasing, PPI is in deflation territory, while our forecast of weak consumption for this year and the impact of a stronger zloty in year-on-year terms imply a rather slow recovery of inflation in the second half of 2010. This allows the MPC to stick to its wait-and-see approach."\par \par \uc2 BACKGROUND:\par \par \uc2 * Polish c.bank independence under threat-c.banker [ID:nLDE63P0ZA]\par \par \uc2 * ECB signals concern over Polish cbank profit row [ID:nLDE63M1Q0]\par \par \uc2 * Polish c.bank tackles vacuum after crash, markets calm [ID:nLDE63B25J]\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken zloty [ID:nLDE63816K]\par \par \uc2 * Polish output beats expectations, rate outlook stable [ID:nLDE63J1NG]\par \par \uc2 * Polish retail sales beat forecast, recovery on track [ID:nLDE63M0MR]\par \par \uc2 * Polish inflation slows to 2.6 percent in March [ID:nLDE63E0LV] (Writing by Karolina Slowikowska)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-RATES/ (INSTANT VIEW)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|PX|E|RBN    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100501e64s0005w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
