\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 4-Greek aid news boosts region, zloty rangebound\b0\par\par\uc2 821 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2010\par 16:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * News on Greek aid activation lifts \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Region's bond markets show no major reaction\par \par \uc2 * Zloty down, risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains\par \par \uc2 (Updates throughout)\par \par \uc2 By Krisztina Than and Dagmara Leszkowicz\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST/WARSAW, April 23 (Reuters) - Emerging Europe's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly higher on Friday, rallying after debt-choked Greece requested the activation of a multi-billion euro EU/IMF-led aid package.\par \par \uc2 The country appealed to the EU and the International Monetary Fund for emergency loans aimed at pulling it out of a debt crisis and easing fears of a default.\par \par \uc2 "This is good information and if market players can be confident about this (agreement), it should definitely provide support for our region," said one Warsaw-based dealer.\par \par \uc2 Central and eastern European assets have not been significantly impacted by Greece's debt woes so far, thanks to the region's relatively buoyant growth outlook and low debt and budget deficit levels.\par \par \uc2 However, worries about the heavily-indebted euro zone periphery have dampened investor appetite towards the region in recent days.\par \par \uc2 By 1355 GMT, the Romanian leu <EURRON=> had strengthened 0.3 percent against the euro and Hungary's forint <EURHUF=> edged up 0.2 percent. The Czech crown <EURCZK=> was flat.\par \par \uc2 ZLOTY UNDERPERFORMS\par \par \uc2 The zloty <EURPLN=> fell 0.3 percent. Dealers said Polish March retail sales data, though much better than expected, did not have a significant impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .[ID:nLDE63M0MR]\par \par \uc2 "Everyone sees Poland's economy is doing well and all the positive news has been already priced in," said another dealer from Warsaw bank.\par \par \uc2 Some market players said the zloty's recent rangebound performance, despite having room to appreciate further -- reflected concerns over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised markets earlier this month with its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since introducing a free float in 2000 to temper the surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's impact on exports and the economy overall.\par \par \uc2 A Reuters polls of analysts showed the zloty could gain some 3 percent in the next 12 months. [ID:nLDE6380S7]\par \par \uc2 The region's stocks extended recent gains, with most indices rising around 1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Bond markets hardly reacted to the Greek news, with only Hungarian paper gaining slightly.\par \par \uc2 Hungarian dealers said the market was still optimistic about the outlook for the forint, which could get a boost from Sunday's run-off parliamentary elections if the centre-right Fidesz party -- which won the first round -- extends its gains to the two-thirds majority that would give it a mandate to implement major reforms.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to cut rates by another 25 basis points on Monday to a new all-time low of 5.25 percent. [ID:nLDE63K1XG] [ID:nLDE63K2J8] \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b