\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Hit by profit-taking; EM debt in demand\b0\par\par\uc2 800 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2010\par 13:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Emerging stocks down almost 1 pct on risk aversion\par \par \uc2 * Polish zloty slips 0.5 pct as investors book profits\par \par \uc2 * Argentina unveils debt swap; more emerging issuance seen\par \par \uc2 By Sujata Rao\par \par \uc2 LONDON, April 16 (Reuters) - Emerging stocks posted their biggest one-day fall in a month on Friday after weak U.S jobs data raised questions over the pace of economic recovery, but emerging bond issuance continued unabated.\par \par \uc2 Emerging assets have been fairly resilient to worries about Greek debt amid good growth data in China and the developing world, a raft of strong corporate results, and the likelihood of low interest rates in the core markets for some time to come.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said markets were taking a breather before the weekend after a strong run of recent gains that saw investors push emerging equities up over 3 percent since the start of April and absorb huge amounts of new bond issuance including from higher-risk names Ukraine and Dubai.\par \par \uc2 MSCI emerging equities fell 0.9 percent, edging away from the previous session's 19-1/2 month highs <.MSCIEF> while most emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled back against the dollar and the euro.\par \par \uc2 "There's clearly some profit-taking but markets have done pretty well in recent days. \uc2 Google\uc2 's results, which came after hours, beat expectations but investors may be reacting to the performance of the shares before the results," said John Lomax, head of emerging equity strategy at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 "The outlook is positive," he added.\par \par \uc2 On \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Polish zloty fell half a percent against the euro, <EURPLN=> underperforming its regional peers as investors stayed wary of more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  following its action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last week.\par \par \uc2 The country's finance minister said on Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  may need to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID: nLDE63D17C]\par \par \uc2 Data showing consumer inflation slowing in March was also zloty-negative, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains one of the best performing emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, with gains of almost 6 percent. "Everywhere people are selling risk and that is affecting emerging markets," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. "The zloty is seen as more vulnerable after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and now, the verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  .... people are rushing to protect profits."\par \par \uc2 A stronger dollar forced the Turkish lira off its highest levels in almost three months <TRY=>. Investors have been piling into the lira following a moderation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ultra-dovish stance, with some expecting a rate rise by June. The lira is up almost 3 percent since the start of April.\par \par \uc2 BONDS ON A ROLL\par \par \uc2 On bond markets, Argentina announced a long-awaited debt swap, offering new bonds and cash to holders of $20 billion in defaulted debt, but investors saw the deal as less generous than expected. [ID:nN15183384].\par \par \uc2 The deal is expected to have a high take-up rate however and could pave the way for the country to return to global capital markets. Argentina credit default swaps failed to react, quoted at 12.6 percent on an upfront basis.\par \par \uc2 Emerging sovereign bond spreads over U.S. Treasuries rose 2 bps as Treasury yields fell but Argentine spreads fell 7 bps.\par \par \uc2 Emerging debt markets are seeing a heavy issuance surge, with sovereigns as well as corporates trying to get funding done while core yields remain low and risk appetite high.\par \par \uc2 Russia wraps up its roadshow next week and fund managers said it may issue $7-$10 billion in two or three tranches in what will be its first bond in a decade.\par \par \uc2 But less desirable credits are also in demand. State-run entities from Dubai and Ukraine, where quasi-sovereigns recently restructured debt, successfully tapped markets this week. Kazakstan's \uc2 Kazmunaigaz\uc2  picked banks for a dollar bond.\par \par \uc2 Both Ukreximbank and Dubai's DEWA paid significant 120-180 bps premiums over the sovereign, the likely reason why DEWA's $1 billion bond got $11 billion in orders. Ukreximbank's $500 million issue was eight times subscribed, sources said.\par \par \uc2 "The market is looking for yield but yields are low in general and we have to invest somewhere," one fund manager said.\par \par \uc2 That view was backed up by data from EPFR Global which showed inflows into emerging bond funds at a weekly record of $1.8 billion. Click on [ID: nLDE63F0GE].\par \par \uc2 But others expressed concern.\par \par \uc2 "I am getting really concerned at the feeding frenzy rebuilding again... as investors dash to get a slice of new issues, and especially as these seem to be moving back down the credit curve in the hunt again for yield," Tim Ash, RBS head of emerging European research, said in a note.\par \par \uc2 (additional reporting by Sebastian Tong; editing by John Stonestreet)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|PX|HX|CZS|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100419e64g000t4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
