\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ/New Europe:  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2  Ready for More  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention \highlight\uc2  Despite Crash\b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2010\par 17:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This article has been posted on New Europe, The Wall Street Journal Online's site for news and analysis on Central and Eastern Europe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Posted by Marcin Sobczyk \f28 \par \par \uc2 The National Bank of Poland, just days after the crash of the presidential airplane, which killed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor and the country's president, is back on its feet and ready for more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the zloty.\par \par \uc2 On the last day in the life of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Slawomir Skrzypek, the NBP bought an undisclosed amount of euros on the market, showing it's ready to act to weaken what it believed was a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthening too quickly.\par \par \uc2 A Monetary Policy Council member said Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to reduce volatility caused by speculative investors. \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , an investment bank, now says the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a much bigger scale than on Apr. 9 if the zloty continues to rise against core \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This didn't seem immediately obvious when Skrzypek died Saturday with 95 others in the presidential airplane crash. Questions over succession at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and over its power to act, started soon after.\par \par \uc2 After the death of Slawomir Skrzypek, first deputy Piotr Wiesiolek took over as the head of the bank's management, in line with the law. But the governor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a dual role in the bank and also acts as a member and chairperson of the Monetary Policy Council. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law makes no mention on who assumes this role in case of the governor's death.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the policy council met and decided that it would give the acting governor full voting power and the authority to schedule meetings for the council--matters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation doesn't discuss. It didn't adopt a document to this effect--it just discussed various interpretations of the law and unanimously agreed, without voting or signing anything, that one of those interpretations would now be considered correct.\par \par \uc2 Amid the chaos, some argued the council doesn't even have that power and that no-one now has the right to schedule policy meetings. But the law says three or more members of the council can also decide to formally schedule the council's monthly meeting, which put those concerns to rest.\par \par \uc2 So, zloty speculators should better brace for more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to move, should it deem such a step necessary.\par \par \uc2 -For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 . [ 16-04-10 1527GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100416e64g0016e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
