\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 3-Polish CPI slows in March to 2.6 pct as fcast\b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2010\par 14:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, April 15 (Reuters) - Polish consumer prices inflation <PLCPIY=ECI> slowed in March from the previous month, statistics office data showed on Thursday, confirming expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep interest rates unchanged this month.\par \par \uc2 The data showed consumer prices rose 2.6 percent year-on-year in March, in line with analysts' forecasts and down from 2.9 percent in February.\par \par \uc2 On a monthly basis <PLCPIM=ECI>, CPI stood at 0.3 percent, against 0.2 percent for February.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said they expected further declines in CPI in coming months due partly to an annual base effect before strengthening domestic demand starts to exert upward pressure on prices again.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council (MPC) is not expected to raise rates until the latter part of the year.\par \par \uc2 *************************************************************\par \par \uc2 FORECAST:\par \par \uc2 Analysts polled by Reuters expected:\par \par \uc2 * March inflation at 2.6 percent year-on-year and 0.4 percent in month-on-month terms.\par \par \uc2 KEY POINTS:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  CPI (percentage change)  March 2010  Feb 2010  March 2009\par  year-on-year                2.6        2.9         3.6\par  \par  month-on-month              0.3        0.2         0.4\par  \par    * revised \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET REACTION:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Polish zloty <EURPLN=D3> <PLN=> and bonds were unchanged immediately after the data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ANALYSTS COMMENTS:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MACIEJ RELUGA, CHIEF ECONOMIST AT BZ WBK IN WARSAW\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think the inflation data will not affect the market or the thinking of the Monetary Policy Council about interest rates. The trend of easing inflation clearly started last month and March is the second consecutive month for inflation to fall.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think the next months will bring a continuation of the trend and that inflation will slow to below 2 percent by mid-2010.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think year-end inflation will be close to March levels."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MATEUSZ SZCZUREK, CHIEF ECONOMIST AT ING BANK:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Core inflation at 2.0-2.1 percent remains almost unchanged. There are no big surprises in any of the sub-categories. We are still in a phase of waiting for the inflation falls to stop. This phase will last about 4-5 months. Only after that the discussion on possible rate hikes will begin."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PETER ATTARD MONTALTO, ECONOMIST AT NOMURA IN LONDON\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "CPI should continue to ease to a base of around 2.3 percent in May before remaining broadly flat and then starting to rise back up to the top end of its target band in Q3 as domestic demand pressures start to become more evident and recent commodity price increases feed through."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Long-run inflation is still seen remaining broadly around target with risks to the upside in our forcast, given demand side pressures and credit expansion through the recovery."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GRZEGORZ MALISZEWSKI, CHIEF ECONOMIST AT MILLENNIUM BANK\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The data is in line with market expectations and is the effect of a high statistical base from last year. We had a hike of regulated prices and a weakening of the zloty last year that boosted prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The data is neutral for the market. It just confirms that the consumer price index is continuing to ease and this should continue further."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BACKGROUND: * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may still need \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - finmin [ID:nLDE63D17C]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Polish macroeconomic forecasts for April [ID:nLDE6381L5]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb zloty, sets precedent [ID:nLDE63816K]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may hike rates before changing bias -cbanker [ID:nLDE6361OM]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Compiled by Dagmara Leszkowicz)\f28 \par \par \uc2 POLAND-INFLATION/ (INSTANT VIEW 3)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|PX|E|RBN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100418e64f0007x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
