\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2  may still need  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  -finmin\b0\par\par\uc2 By Pawel Sobczak and Piotr Bujnicki   \par \uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 2010\par 13:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with deputy finmin, trader comment)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, April 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  may continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, a deputy finance minister said on Wednesday, contradicting earlier comments from an economic aide to Prime Minister Donald Tusk.\par \par \uc2 Deputy Finance Minister Dominik Radziwill's remarks helped trim some of the zloty's previous gains sparked by aide Michal Boni's suggestion that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , used recently to weaken the Polish unit, may not be needed.\par \par \uc2 "We will be actively cooperating with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ... We do not rule out that the finance ministry may also be buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market," Dominik Radziwill told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 "They (investors) have to take into account the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Radziwill's views seem closer to those of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, who have indicated that the death of bank governor Slawomir Skrzypek, along with President Lech Kaczynski and dozens of other top officials in a plane crash last weekend, would not impact \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 Last Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time since the country adopted a free float \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime in 2000.\par \par \uc2 The bank started buying euros, weakening the Polish unit by 1 percent against the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a move welcomed by the finance ministry, which has often complained about the negative impact of a strong zloty on a still fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 At 1528 GMT the euro traded at 3.8605 zlotys, 0.3 percent lower than on Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 "Radziwill's comments slightly weakened the zloty but this situation does not make Boni look good," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a Warsaw bank said.\par \par \uc2 "Suddenly Boni speaks against the Monetary Policy Council, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the interests of the economy. And no one knows why, especially as there had been signals from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , MPC and finance ministry that they actually may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." (Additional reporting by Kuba Jaworowski, writing by Karolina Slowikowska and Kuba Jaworowski)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-ZLOTY/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|PX|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100414e64e000ov\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
