\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 4- \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gain; zloty  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears ease\b0\par\par\uc2 993 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 2010\par 17:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Crown, forint benefit from long zloty cross unwinds\par \par \uc2 * Forint extends post-election rally, bonds correct\par \par \uc2 * Zloty supported by PM aide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments\par \par \uc2 * Prague stocks jump, near pre-crisis levels\par \par \uc2 (Adds Polish finmin comments)\par \par \uc2 By Dagmara Leszkowicz and Marius Zaharia\par \par \uc2 WARSAW/BUCHAREST, April 14 (Reuters) - The Czech crown hit a seven-month peak and Hungary's forint climbed to one-month highs on Wednesday, tracking global equities, while the zloty rose as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears eased.\par \par \uc2 Strategists expect a recovery in central European exports will help fuel gains this year in the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have already rallied since the beginning of 2010, while strong corporate results have also boosted sentiment.\par \par \uc2 But questions have arisen on whether stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could hurt recovery prospects and the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised markets last Friday with its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since introducing a free float in 2000.\par \par \uc2 The prime minister's top economic adviser Michal Boni said on Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  further in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. [ID:nLDE63D17C] Later, deputy finance minister Dominik Radziwill said investors should still take the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  into account. [ID:nWSF008941]\par \par \uc2 At 1530 GMT, the zloty <EURPLN=> was bid 0.3 percent up on the day at 3.859 per euro and was little changed after Radziwill's comments. Dealers said Boni's comments may suggest the bank has not yet decided to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  further.\par \par \uc2 The forint <EURHUF=>, the crown <EURCZK=> and Romania's leu <EURRON=> were all up 0.2-0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 While the zloty's appreciation will likely cool in the short term, some analysts say markets will probably push the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  into another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength you get in this current economic environment, the more these economies will be at risk of disappointing readings ... and slowdown in growth momentum," said Michal Dybula, economist for central and eastern Europe at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . "They will not hesitate to use (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )."\par \par \uc2 The zloty's reversal, after rallying more than 6 percent gains this year, has boosted peers the crown and forint as investors square long zloty positions against them.\par \par \uc2 The forint and Hungarian bonds have rallied this week after a sweeping first round election win for the centre-right Fidesz party, which gained a near two-thirds majority needed to push through vital reforms. [ID:nLDE63107B]\par \par \uc2 Markets still price in a 25 basis point interest rate cut on April 26, one day after the election's second round. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's minutes indicated that the end of the rate-cutting cycle was uncertain. [ID:nLDE63D1ID]\par \par \uc2 "I think the cuts will continue further, perhaps even below 5 percent," one dealer in Budapest said.\par \par \uc2 Bond yields ticked up on profit taking after dropping around 50 basis points since Sunday's election.\par \par \uc2 POLAND RESILIENT\par \par \uc2 Polish markets have held up following the Saturday crash of a government plane that killed President Lech Kaczynski, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Slawomir Skrzypek and other senior officials.\par \par \uc2 The bank's acting governor Piotr Wiesiolek told daily Gazeta Wyborcza on Wednesday the country should name a new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head without unnecessary delays. [ID:nLDE63D04J]\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 * For stories on the Polish crash and its aftermath please double click on [ID:nLDE63C11O]\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Polish bonds trimmed some of their previous gains, but were still stronger compared to Tuesday's levels. Poland sold 3.51 billion zlotys worth of 10-year bonds in a well-bid primary tender on Wednesday. [ID:nWSF008935]\par \par \uc2 The Prague bourse <.PX> jumped almost 3 percent to levels last seen at the start of the financial crisis in September 2008, led by a 21.4 percent rise in miner New World Resources after the company booked much higher contract prices over the next year. [ID:nLDE63D0EN] \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                            change   change\par                                            today    in 2010 \par Czech crown      <EURCZK=>   25.054   25.113  +0.24%   +5.05%\par Polish zloty     <EURPLN=>    3.859    3.871  +0.31%   +6.35%\par Hungarian forint <EURHUF=>  262.26   263.6    +0.51%   +3.08%\par Croatian kuna    <EURHRK=>    7.256   