\par\par \b \uc2 FOCUS: Polish Zloty, Bonds Stable Despite Tragedy\b0\par\par\uc2 458 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2010\par 11:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Malgorzata Halaba \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--Poland's zloty and Treasury bonds are stable despite Saturday's tragedy when President Lech Kaczynski, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's head Slawomir Skrzypek, and a large part of political elite died in a plane crash.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The zloty is clearly supported by Sunday news on the European Union aid package for Greece and any possible uncertainty is related to fears \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , economists said.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after the opening Monday the zloty weakened against the euro, to above the 3.88 level, but immediately came back to Friday afternoon levels.\par \par \uc2 At 0836 GMT, EUR/PLN traded at 3.87 from 3.88 Friday afternoon and the average yield on a five-year benchmark treasury bond was at 5.14% from 5.17% Friday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 "The tragedy had no impact on the market," said Maja Goettig, chief economist at \uc2 Bank BPH\uc2  in Warsaw, seeing early Monday's weakening as an aftermath of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than the reaction to the tragedy.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market for the first time since the zloty was floated ten years ago.\par \par \uc2 Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the zloty weakened to around 3.90 against the euro, from 3.8450, but was back at around 3.88 Friday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 "Now the investors might be careful because further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot be excluded," Goetting said, adding that clearly the investors show strong trust in Poland's legal procedures which will ensure there is no risk for the function of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Despite the tragic events on Saturday, we believe any negative implications for financial markets will be short lived, given continuity in both the government and the National Bank of Poland," Piotr Kalisz, chief economist at \uc2 Citibank Handlowy\uc2  in Warsaw, wrote in his research note.\par \par \uc2 Economists pointed out that the responsibilities of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governor were taken by Skrzypek's first deputy, Piotr Wiesiolek.\par \par \uc2 And while it's quite possible Skrzypek's successor may be appointed only after the presidential election, this "should not be a reason for concern for the financial markets," \uc2 Bank Zachodni WBK\uc2  said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 "Over the longer term we remain bullish given that economic policy is unchanged and the fact that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone is rarely, if ever, sufficient to do more than slow the pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement," \uc2 Royal Bank of Canada\uc2  said Sunday. "We still look for a move to 3.75-3.80 (against the euro) in the second half of the year."\par \par \uc2 By Malgorzata Halaba, Dow Jones Newswires, +48 22 447-24-30; malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com [ 12-04-10 0900GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5008    \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100412e64c000tq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
