\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Polish markets to stabilise after plane disaster\b0\par\par\uc2 849 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2010\par 17:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * After early nervousness, impact likely to be minor\par \par \uc2 * Fiscal, most economic policy in hands of cabinet\par \par \uc2 * Interest rate path unlikely to change\par \par \uc2 * Next c.bank governor may not be so keen on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Marcin Goclowski and Chris Borowski\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, April 11 (Reuters) - Polish markets are expected to stabilise quickly after early jitters following the deaths of the country's president and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rate policy unlikely to show any immediate change.\par \par \uc2 Poland's economic stewardship is mainly in the hands of Prime Minister Donald Tusk and his cabinet, who have maintained growth during the global credit crisis. President Lech Kaczynski played only a secondary, mainly ceremonial role.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Slawomir Skrzypek, also killed by Saturday's plane crash in Russia, was seen as the driving force behind last Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt strengthening of the zloty.\par \par \uc2 His replacement could eventually modify that policy, but the new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief may not be chosen for some weeks, during which time current policy should continue. Interest rate policy, which has been broadly supported by the entire 10-member Monetary Policy Council, looks set to stay unchanged.\par \par \uc2 So while the zloty may weaken slightly when markets reopen on Monday, perhaps to its lows late last month of around 3.90 against the euro, and government bonds could be sold modestly, the markets are not expected to establish new trends.\par \par \uc2 "The financial markets look at this from a longer perspective, so even with a short-term discounting of this tragedy, I don't see a long-term impact on the economy," said former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Dariusz Filar.\par \par \uc2 Marek Juras, head of equity research at \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  CAIB in Warsaw, said: "The stock market should be the least affected, while we could see some more activity initially in the zloty and the bond markets."\par \par \uc2 The Polish stock market has been in a strong uptrend for the past two months, hitting a 21-month high last week, because of expectations for an economic recovery.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  POLICY\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty on Friday was the first since \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced a free float for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2000.\par \par \uc2 Tusk's government backed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fearing a strong zloty could stall the economic recovery, but it might conceivably end up choosing a new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor who is less willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Until the new governor is chosen, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy will be continued by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  management," said Jakub Borowski, chief economist at Invest-Bank. "But the new governor may oppose it, so some investors may expect future zloty strengthening."\par \par \uc2 Also, Skrzypek was reluctant to set a firm target for Poland to adopt the euro; his successor may be more euro-friendly.\par \par \uc2 But it remains unclear when Poland's Acting President Bronislaw Komorowski, a political ally of Tusk, will appoint Skrzypek's successor, because there is uncertainty over the extent of his authority before elections in June.\par \par \uc2 Piotr Wiesiolek, Skrzypek's top deputy, will serve as acting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor until the appointment. Analysts are floating several potential candidates: former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Boguslaw Grabowski, former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Jerzy Pruski, or even Finance Minister Jacek Rostowski.\par \par \uc2 In any case, there is no reason to expect a change of interest rate policy. Skrzypek was once seen as a leading dove on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate-setting body, but in recent months he had moderated his views and had spoken of raising the key rate off its all-time low of 3.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 "The path for interest rates shouldn't change because recent comments by Skrzypek showed that he stopped being a proponent of loose monetary policy, and it's difficut to imagine that a new head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have a more dovish approach," said Borowski.\par \par \uc2 POLITICAL TENSIONS\par \par \uc2 In the long term, the replacement of Skrzypek is likely to ease a tense relationship between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government, and between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor and other members of the Monetary Policy Council. This could be moderately positive for all the financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Most of the council were appointed by Poland's centre-right government earlier this year. Skrzypek by contrast was appointed in 2007 by Kaczynski, a founder of main opposition party Law and Justice.\par \par \uc2 In particular, Skrzypek's replacement may end a conflict over the government's demand that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hand over as much as 8 billion zlotys ($2.8 billion) in last year's earnings to the state coffers to help cover the budget deficit.\par \par \uc2 "This completely changes the dynamics between the bank and the government in the dispute over what to do with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's profits," said an emerging markets analyst at a foreign institution, who asked not to be named.\par \par \uc2 Skrzypek had clashed with the government and members of the council over reclassifying the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to beef up its earnings. (Editing by Andrew Torchia)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-CRASH/MARKETS (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100411e64b000cg\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (poland near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\asp